# Story 10.8 live-validation artifacts.
#
# What is committed: everything that re-derives or adjudicates a number — the driver
# (`measure_fallbacks.py`), the pre-registration (`README.md`) and the raw measurement
# ledger (`measurements.jsonl`). All of it is text and all of it is small; a reader can
# check every claim in the spec's `## Auto Run Result` from this directory alone,
# without a GPU and without re-running the pipeline.
#
# What is ignored: rendered frames and clips. NONE EXIST YET — the before/after render
# (story AC9) is blocked on ComfyUI being up and on Jay watching it, so this directory
# currently holds no image at all. The rules are written now so the follow-up run drops
# its output into an already-decided split instead of inventing one:
#
#   - commit the adjudication images the verdict cites, downscaled to ~512 px on the
#     long edge — "which way is the figure facing" survives that easily. Name them
#     `before_after.*`, `*_pair.*` or `grid_*.*`: those three are what the rules below
#     un-ignore, in any image format;
#   - ignore the raw per-shot renders and full videos they were built from, which are
#     regenerable from the committed driver against the same run.
#
# `git status --porcelain` on this directory proves nothing (it is ignored by design).
# Assert file state with `find _bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/10-8-live-validation
# -type f` plus dates. Never blanket-delete an ignored payload here: video.py unlinks
# shot clips on re-render, so a rendered leg can be the only surviving copy.

# Ignore the raw payload by extension, then un-ignore the adjudication sheets by NAME.
# The names, not the format: the sibling 10-1b rules negated `*_pair.jpg` / `grid_*.jpg`
# against a `*.png` ignore, so every negation there was a no-op and nothing said the
# sheets had to be JPEG. Copied here, they would have silently swallowed the
# `before_after.png` this story's follow-up is specified to drop in — in a directory
# whose own header warns that `git status` proves nothing.
*.mp4
*.png
*.jpg

!before_after.*
!*_pair.*
!grid_*.*
